return {h=20,w=1300,cr=125,hc=40,bh=70,gr="fast-then-very-slow",eg={"ground","water2"},st={130,70,35,70,35,60},ab={{41,0},{12,0},{46,1}},genus={en="Ball Whale Pokémon",es="Pokémon Ballenabola",pt="Pokémon Baleia Bola"},flavor={en={[7]="WAILMER’s nostrils are located above its eyes. This playful Pokémon loves to startle people by forcefully snorting out seawater it stores inside its body out of its nostrils.",[8]="WAILMER can store water inside its body to transform itself into a ball for bouncing around on the ground. By filling itself up with more water, this Pokémon can elevate the height of its bounces.",[9]="While this Pokémon usually lives in the sea, it can survive on land, although not too long. It loses vitality if its body becomes dried out.",[10]="When it sucks in a large volume of seawater, it becomes like a big, bouncy ball. It eats a ton of food daily.",[11]="When it sucks in a large volume of seawater, it becomes like a big, bouncy ball. It eats a ton of food daily.",[12]="On sunny days, it lands on beaches to bounce like a ball and play. It spouts water from its nose.",[13]="On sunny days, it lands on beaches to bounce like a ball and play. It spouts water from its nose.",[14]="On sunny days, it lands on beaches to bounce like a ball and play. It spouts water from its nose.",[15]="It bounces playfully like a ball. The more seawater it swallows, the higher it bounces.",[16]="It bounces playfully like a ball. The more seawater it swallows, the higher it bounces.",[17]="On sunny days, it lands on beaches to bounce like a ball and play. It spouts water from its nose.",[18]="On sunny days, it lands on beaches to bounce like a ball and play. It spouts water from its nose.",[21]="It eats one ton of food every day. It plays by shooting stored seawater out its blowholes with great force.",[22]="It eats one ton of food every day. It plays by shooting stored seawater out its blowholes with great force.",[23]="It bounces playfully like a ball. The more seawater it swallows, the higher it bounces.",[24]="It eats one ton of food every day. It plays by shooting stored seawater out its blowholes with great force.",[25]="Wailmer’s nostrils are located above its eyes. This playful Pokémon loves to startle people by forcefully snorting out seawater it stores inside its body out of its nostrils.",[26]="Wailmer can store water inside its body to transform itself into a ball for bouncing around on the ground. By filling itself up with more water, this Pokémon can elevate the height of its bounces.",[27]="It loves to startle people. It fills itself up with seawater and plays by bouncing around like a ball.",[28]="It shows off by spraying jets of seawater from the nostrils above its eyes. It eats a solid ton of Wishiwashi every day.",[29]="It swims along with its mouth open and swallows down seawater along with its food. It sprays excess water out of its nostrils.",[30]="Due to their memories of when they once lived on land, pods of them will, very rarely, wash up on shore.",[33]="It shows off by spraying jets of seawater from the nostrils above its eyes. It eats a solid ton of Wishiwashi every day.",[34]="When it sucks in a large volume of seawater, it becomes like a big, bouncy ball. It eats a ton of food daily."},es={[23]="Le gusta botar como una pelota de playa. Cuanta más agua de mar traga, más alto puede llegar.",[24]="Engulle una tonelada de comida al día. Le gusta jugar expulsando con energía el agua marina por sus espiráculos.",[25]="Wailmer tiene los espiráculos encima de la cabeza. A este juguetón Pokémon le encanta asustar a la gente expulsando el agua que acumula a través de estos orificios.",[26]="Wailmer puede almacenar agua dentro de su organismo para convertirse en una pelota y botar por tierra firme. Cuanta más agua trague, mayor altura alcanzará al saltar.",[27]="A este Pokémon le gusta dar sustos a la gente. Se divierte tragando mucha agua de mar para hincharse como una bola y dar grandes saltos.",[28]="Wailmer se c